 "brief": "Proton Stability in Grand Unified Theories, in Strings and in Branes — A broad overview of the current status of proton stability in uni- ﬁed models of particle interactions is given which includes",
 "extended": "**Proton Stability in Grand Unified Theories, in Strings and in Branes**\n\n*Grand Unified Theories*\n\n258 pp, 62 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** A broad overview of the current status of proton stability in uni- ﬁed models of particle interactions is given which includes non - su- persymmetric uniﬁcation, SUSY and SUGRA uniﬁed models, uniﬁ- cation based on extra dimensions, and string-M-theory models. The extra dimensional uniﬁcation includes 5D and 6D and universal extra dimensional (UED) models, and models based on warped geometry. Proton stability in a wide array of string theory and M theory models is reviewed. These include Calabi-Yau models, grand uniﬁed models with Kac-Moody levels k > 1, a new class of heterotic string models, models based on intersecting D branes, and string landscape models. The destabilizing eﬀect of quantum gravity on the proton is discussed. The possibility of testing grand uniﬁed models, models based on extra dimensions and string-M-theory models via their distinctive modes is investigated.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Experimental bounds and future searches; 3 Nucleon decay in non-supersymmetric scenario; 3.1 Baryon number violation in the Standard Mo; 3.2 Grand unification and gauge contributions ; 3.3 Proton decay induced by scalar leptoquarks; 4 Nucleon decay in SUSY and SUGRA unified theo; 4.1 R-parity violation and the decay of the pr; 4.2 Supersymmetry breaking and SUGRA unificati; 4.3 Effect of CP violating phases on proton li; 4.4 Doublet-triplet splitting problem; 4.5 Proton decay in $SU(5)$ supersymmetric gra; 4.6 Nucleon decay in SO(10) theories; 4.7 Proton decay in models with unified symmet; 5 Testing grand unification; 5.1 Textures, Planck scale effects and proton ; 5.2 Gravitational smearing effects",
